"{\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"There are no complete award journeys among the selected search results, so I can’t recommend a complete award itinerary from these records. If you prefer economy and are considering Alaska miles, I’d check the January 1 lead first: among the two shown Alaska leads, it reports the lower points amount. Its schedule is only date-level, though, and the reported seat count does not confirm that the award can be booked for you. The January 9 United lead is another economy option to check if that date or program better fits your plans; its points cannot be directly compared with Alaska’s.\"},{\"k\":\"l\",\"r\":\"A3@2027-01-01/SFO>BKK/E\",\"n\":\"January 1 — Alaska economy award lead\",\"v\":\"This SFO–BKK award summary reports 42,500 Alaska miles and USD 50.90 in award taxes, with quote scope unknown. It reports 8 seats and lists AS and JX, but gives only the date, not a flight schedule; leg cabins are not specified. The request is for one traveler, but no returned traveler count is reported, so the seat figure does not verify support for the request or current availability.\"},{\"k\":\"l\",\"r\":\"A26@2027-01-09/SFO>BKK/E\",\"n\":\"January 9 — United economy award lead\",\"v\":\"This SFO–BKK award summary reports 55,000 United miles and USD 16.20 in award taxes, with quote scope unknown. It reports 9 seats and lists B6, BR, CA, ET, SQ, UA and ZH; the schedule is date-only and leg cabins are not specified. The reported USD 16.20 quote is lower than the USD 50.90 reported for the January 1 Alaska lead, but both scopes are unknown, so this is only a raw quote comparison—not a trip-total or like-for-like cost comparison. No returned traveler count is reported.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"If premium economy matters more than minimizing Alaska points, the January 12 Alaska lead is the shown cabin alternative. It reports 140,000 Alaska miles—97,500 more than the January 1 Alaska economy lead—and the same reported USD 50.90 in award taxes, both with unknown quote scope. The reported seat count does not resolve the missing schedule or verify booking support.\"},{\"k\":\"l\",\"r\":\"A37@2027-01-12/SFO>BKK/P\",\"n\":\"January 12 — Alaska premium economy award lead\",\"v\":\"This SFO–BKK award summary reports premium economy, 140,000 Alaska miles, USD 50.90 in award taxes with unknown scope, and 9 seats. JX is listed as the carrier. It provides a date but no schedule, and does not specify cabin by leg; no returned traveler count is reported.\"},{\"k\":\"b\",\"r\":\"C1@2027-01-01T22:55-08:00/SFO>BKK\",\"n\":\"January 1 — Cathay Pacific cash-fare baseline\",\"v\":\"The cash itinerary is SFO–HKG–BKK, with one stop; it departs January 1 at 10:55 p.m. San Francisco time and arrives January 4 at 10:35 a.m. Bangkok time. Reported elapsed time is 44 hours 40 minutes. The source cash fare is USD 640.00 with unknown quote scope, so it is not established as a per-person, party-total, or all-in price. The record reports one traveler for this cash itinerary; that does not establish the scope of its fare quote or make it comparable to award taxes.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"The selected award leads are not complete itineraries: none supplies flight times or enough schedule detail to assess the routing. The search results are partial, with some route/date detail queries omitted and related searches incomplete; the selected examples should not be read as the full set of possibilities. Check the booking program for exact flights, current award availability for one traveler, cabin by leg, and final taxes and fees before deciding.\"}]}"
